 palace of Shushan (Esther 9:9).","verses":1,"father":"Haman","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"haman_1360","name":"Haman","also":"","summary":"(of Persian origin), magnificent, the name of the vizier (i.e., the prime minister) of the Persian king Ahasuerus (Esther 3:1, etc.). He is called an “Agagite,” which seems to denote that he was descended from the royal family of the Amalekites, the bitterest enemies of the Jews, as Agag was one of the titles of the Amalekite kings.","verses":45,"father":"Hammedatha","mother":"","v":[10,12,13,14,24]},{"id":"hammedatha_1362","name":"Hammedatha","also":"","summary":"Father of Haman, designated usually “the Agagite” (Esther 3:1, 10; 8:5).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10,24]},{"id":"esther_1343","name":"Esther","also":"Hadassah","summary":"The queen of Ahasuerus, and heroine of the book that bears her name. She was a Jewess named Hadas’sah (the myrtle), but when she entered the royal harem she received the name by which she henceforth became known (Esther 2:7).","verses":46,"father":"Abihail","mother":"","v":[12,13,25,29,31,32]},{"id":"abihail_32","name":"Abihail","also":"","summary":"The father of Esther and uncle of Mordecai (Esther 2:15).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]}],"places":[{"id":"susa_1118","name":"Susa","kind":"City","lat":32.19202,"lon":48.24854,"summary":"A lily, the Susa of Greek and Roman writers, once the capital of Elam. It lay in the uplands of Susiana, on the east of the Tigris, about 150 miles to the north of the head of the Persian Gulf.","verses":20,"v":[6,11,12,13,14,15,18]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[7969,7969,7969,3117,8147,8147,8147,2320,2320,2320,143,143,4428,4428,1697,1881,1881,6213,6213,6213,6213,3117,3117,3117,341,341,3064,3064,3064,7663,7663,7980,7980,0,2015,2015,2015,2015,2015,3064,3064,3064,7980,1992,8130,8130,8130],[3605,3605,4082,4082,4082,4428,4428,325,3064,3064,6950,5892,5892,5892,7971,7971,1245,1245,1245,7451,7451,7451,